    "JurisdictionSpecifics": "California Penal Code Section 187 defines murder as the unlawful killing of a human being with malice aforethought. First-degree murder requires premeditation and deliberation, or the killing of a person during the commission of certain felonies. Self-defense is a legal privilege when the defendant reasonably believes deadly force is necessary to prevent imminent death or great bodily harm.",
